// Code signing — the one build setting that is NOT generated.
//
// The .xcodeproj is produced by `xcodegen generate` from project.yml, so anything set in Xcode's
// Signing & Capabilities tab is thrown away the next time the project is regenerated. That is what
// kept re-breaking signing: a team ID was hardcoded in project.yml, and every regeneration put it
// back regardless of what Xcode had been told.
//
// This file is a plain xcconfig. xcodegen references it and never rewrites it, so whatever you set
// here survives.
//
// Aimee's personal team, read from the provisioning profile Xcode actually issued.
//
// The previous value (BNV6X8W4QS) came from an old signing certificate sitting in the keychain and
// was never a team Xcode could use — hence "No Account for Team BNV6X8W4QS" on every build.
//
// If this ever goes stale, the true value is in Xcode → Settings → Accounts next to the team name,
// or from a profile on disk:
//
//   security cms -D -i ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/UserData/Provisioning\ Profiles/*.mobileprovision \
//     | plutil -extract TeamIdentifier json -o - -
//
// Note: a free personal team means an installed build stops launching after 7 days. Rebuilding
// from Xcode renews it — that is expected, not a bug.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = CQ892K6L4F
